  {
    "insert": "An example is a great way to show the severity of the problem. By expanding the example briefly drawing the scenario the challenges and hurdles students that do stay behind are facing due to the \"one-size-fits-all\" curriculum you can reinforce the effect and highlight the impact LLM agents could make by being the necessary tool to improve the learning experience.\n\nYour anchor in the third paragraph of your motivation has the goal to present how the problem was dealt so far, the domain of the problem, it's relevance in academia and highlighting the deficits of the current literature concering LLM agents as an \"always-present teacher\".\nYou've demonstrated the domain of the problem in your second paragraph with the \"one-size-fits-all\" example. You showcase in your third paragraph the potential use cases where the LLM agents could be deployed and used. This can create the connection to the relevance of the topic in academia by referencing sources that showed that there is an existing problem to the current situation of meeting the demand for individual support for students. Since it is not mentioned how the problem was dealt with so far and does not visible highlight the deficits, I suggest you to ask the team of the module \"Einführung ins wissenschaftlliche Arbeiten\" for recommendations [REMOVED] In that way you can improve you anchor.\n\n\nIn your second chapter the approach the goal is to showcase how you are planning to tackle your research questions. In order to do this successfully you need to be specific on what methodologies you use, how you incorporate theory in your research and highlight the current SOTA and how your work is positioned in this domain and benefits the community.\n\nIn your SOTA section you mention Duolingo and Khan Academy which are both reputable learning sources. This is a great connection to the current practical use of how learning is currently being done in the public. The bridge to the research papers of Jyothy et al. and Xu et al. shows that it you also rely on other research sources showing that your understanding of the SOTA is good.\nIt is important to use the sources correctly in order to prove that you understand what you are using. You wrote as the forelast sentence in your SOTA section\n"
